course: dictionary
lesson: 3980
title: Clues in a list of clothes
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words are hard because you have never seen the thing. In «a chauffeur in leather gaiters», the word gaiters comes after leather and describes something a person wears, so gaiters must be a kind of clothing.
explain: Look at the words around it. «Toad in goggles, cap, gaiters, gauntlets and an enormous overcoat» is a list of things worn by a person. Goggles, cap and overcoat are all clothes, so gaiters is probably a clothing word too.
explain: Now test your idea. Swap in a meaning, such as "a cover for the lower leg", and read the sentence again: «Toad in goggles, cap, a cover for the lower leg, gauntlets and an enormous overcoat». If it still makes sense, your meaning fits.
fact: A gaiter is a cover worn over the ankle and lower leg.
fact: Walkers and hikers wear gaiters to keep mud and snow out of their boots.
fact: In old stories, «gaiters» can mean leather leggings worn by bishops, soldiers and gentlemen.
fact: In The Wind in the Willows, Toad wears gaiters with his motoring clothes.
fact: A «neck gaiter» is a tube of cloth worn around the neck in winter.
exercise: Why do walkers wear gaiters? | *To keep mud and snow out of their boots | To keep their hats on in the wind | To hear better on the path | To make their boots shine in the sun
exercise: «Toad in goggles, cap, gaiters, gauntlets and an enormous overcoat» — which word is worn on the head? | goggles | overcoat | gaiters | *cap
exercise: Nadia says gaiters must be a kind of car, because of the chauffeur. Why is she wrong? | Chauffeurs always ride in gaiters, so gaiters must be cars | *A chauffeur is a person who drives, and gaiters are worn on the legs | The word gaiters is too long to be clothing | Gaiters and cars are both red
test: What is a neck gaiter? | A shiny red hat | A small car for the country | A leather boot worn by soldiers | *A tube of cloth worn around the neck in winter
test: Old gaiters, worn by soldiers and gentlemen, were made of what? | Paper | *Leather | Glass | Plastic
exam: In «a chauffeur in leather gaiters», which clue tells you what gaiters are made of? | ran | chauffeur | Toad | *leather
